    "turn_text": "Obviously, John Boehner was a speaker. He was had been here a long time, but it kind of goes to a deeper point that I was just making with how people progress over time. John Boehner was part of what they called the gang of seven. People don't realize that. In fact, they may have to Google it, but there's so many gangs in Washington. But again, seven back then, they were taking on the House Post Office. They were taking on the House Bank. And these were special perks that members of Congress actually could take advantage of. And so John Boehner was part of that group that took it on. He had worked his way up to become Speaker. And with that, whenever you concentrate the power in in the speaker's office, whether it's John Boehner or anyone else, it is not good for a representative form of government. So I guess",
