    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think part of it happened just as a natural efficiency mode. You know, so originally, Congress was designed to be a lot more laborious than it is exciting and it's contemporaneous. And so when you look at Congress, it was much easier for there to be a negotiation that happens just with the speaker, the speaker, and the leader of the Senate. I know when I was in the White House, I was surprised at how little input we received from rank and file members. It was all either Leader McConnell Leader Schumer, Speaker Pelosi, or at that time when I was there, we were in the minority in the house, so it would have been Leader McCarthy, but very little input from anybody else. Everybody can say that their pet project was X, Y, or Z. We were talking to the four corners, as they call it, on A, B, and C.",
