    "turn_text": "And he had seen it up close and personal, that the average man and woman on Main Street felt like that Washington DC was no longer fighting for them. And he was willing to fight for the forgotten man and woman. And so to that extent, it actually made a huge difference. And so campaigning with him, it was very different. He's the only guy that I know of that actually his personal plane was nicer than Air Force. So as we traveled obviously across North Carolina being a swing state and one that he had to have, I got to know him and I saw people come from all over. I mean, people would travel hours and hours to show up at a rally because they said finally someone's willing to speak for me. I think the thing that Yeah, there was a union worker, I think I talked to in Pennsylvania. And I said, you know, why is it that you support Donald Trump? And this was actually during his re-elect. And he says, well, he's just like me. Now, this is a",
