  {
    "episode_id": 96855,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96855.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "And so you mentioned Johnny McEntee did a great job of making a number of recommendations to the president for staff changes. But I think the other part of that is it just shows the big machine that's here in Washington, D.C. that if you're not careful, that big machine will consume anybody from senators and House members to the president of the United States. And he, listen, this was a business guy that had never run for office, was coming into the highest office in the land as the 45th president of the United States. And he was getting all kinds of recommendations from different people saying, listen, hire this one. This was a good one. And what do you do as a CEO? You hire people with expertise. Well, you know, in that case, it was just a lot of people that served in previous administration. And all they were doing was biting their time until there was a next Republican administration. And so I think the big discouragement to me was to say, if you came here to actually support what was going to fundamentally change Washington, D.C., why were you trying to do it the old way? And so working through that, certainly looking at a second administration had President Trump had a second administration. I know that we were making plans. Second consecutive administration. Valid. So as we looked at that, we were planning to make some major changes just to make sure that the swamp didn't consume the hopes and dreams of the American people.",
