    "turn_text": "that. Listen, Washington, D.C. is not going to be run as a business because it's a political animal. Are there certain aspects of a business where you can say, sure, let's run it as a business if it's supporting the values of the people back home? But in ways, it is run like a business. It's big business for consultants, for special interest groups. And so the sad part about it is the way that you think about, let's just run it as a business. We can think about it in a good way. But it's really all about big business. It's big business on the people that help with campaigns. It's big business on pollsters. And part of our problem is we send the same message over and over again, paying the same people over and over again. So for me, it's all about actually supporting businesses, small businesses on Main Street. And if you can do that, and do that in a real systemic way, that's what we need to be doing, but operating it like a business. You know, most of the decisions that get here and get made here in Washington, D.C. would be thrown out of most",
